      ":question/problem": "The function $C(t)=6{e}^{-2t}$ gives the concentration, in milligrams per liter, of a medication in the bloodstream $t$ hours after administration. Find the instantaneous rate of change of the concentration as a function of $t.$\n\nThe instantaneous rate of change of the concentration is\n{{field-1}}\nmilligrams per liter per hour."
